strictfp:(strict floating point)
10/6=1.435435
if we declare strictfp of any method ,any class they must follow the some IEE rule to become
java platform independent
strictfp forces Java to give the SAME floating-point result on every machine.
1.the floating point calculations are varied from os and processor to processor
it will generate platform dependent output
2.to overcome above problem to get the platform independent
result use strictfp modifier
3.strictfp modifier is applicable to methods , classes
4. if a method declared as strictfp , inside the method all floating point calculations will fallow IEEE754.
5.if a class declared as strictfp inside the class, all methods will fallow the IEEE754


