variable arguments:
String...
....=allow to take any number of value
Allow method 0-args,1-args,2-args

class Test
{
void m1(int... a)
{
sout("good morning")
}
psvm(String[] args){
Test t=new Test();
t.m1();
t.m1(10);
t.m1(10,20);
t.m1(10,20,30);
}
}
//4 times good morning

... is called varargs (variable-length arguments).

👉 It means:You can pass 0, 1, or many values
Normal main method:public static void main(String[] args)
-args is an array of String
-Size is decided at runtime

Varargs version:public static void main(String... args)
-You can pass any number of String arguments
-Java internally converts it to a String[]
👉 Both are 100% SAME for main()

❌ Rules (exam-important)
Varargs must be last parameter
void test(int a, String... s) // ✅
void test(String... s, int a) // ❌
Only one varargs allowed

